Ladybird computes a media element’s seekable ranges from the attached
MediaSource’s live seekable range and its buffered ranges the way the
spec defines, as the other engines do: Gecko in its MediaSource::
SetLiveSeekableRange() and MediaSourceDecoder::GetSeekableImpl(), WebKit
in MediaSource::setLiveSeekableRange() and MediaSourcePrivate::
seekable(), and Blink in MediaSource::setLiveSeekableRange() and
MediaSource::SeekableInternal(). Each of them returns the union of the
live range and the buffered ranges for an infinite duration.
